Subarchy's Neovim configuration is the LazyVim starter
(https://github.com/LazyVim/starter, Apache License 2.0) with one changed
file, lua/config/lazy.lua (shipped here as subarchy-lazy.lua): the update
checker is off and the bootstrap clone is gone, because the plugins come
prebuilt in this package. Every other file of the starter is unchanged.
LazyVim itself (https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim) is Apache License 2.0.
The cached plugins keep their own licence files in their directories.

lua/config/lazy.lua also keeps /usr/share/nvim/site on the runtime path,
which lazy.nvim's reset would drop, so the system's colour schemes load.

lua/plugins/subarchy.lua is Subarchy's own plugin layer (not from the
starter): the dashboard mark and the colour scheme that follows the active
theme.
